# Published to the public repo root by sync.sh (see tools/sync_stage.py
# ALLOWLIST_FILES). This file exists for people who CLONE the public repo and
# follow the OpenCode setup in the README — that flow generates a tree here.

# OpenCode agent projection: regenerated on demand by
# `crux/scripts/generate-opencode-agents.py`, never shipped in a release.
# Re-run the generator after every pull; see README § OpenCode.
/opencode/

# The arch stack-pack corpus: ten third-party repositories fetched on demand
# by `crux/scripts/tests/arch-corpus/fetch.py`. The script, its `corpus.yml`
# manifest and the documented fetch command all ship publicly, so a clone of
# the public repo that runs the fetch lands ~79 MB of other people's source —
# their `.git` directories included — inside this working tree. Without this
# rule a `git add -A` stages all of it under this repo's licence. The clones
# are reproducible from the pinned SHAs in `corpus.yml`; nothing here is
# authored content.
.cache/

# Local plugin/session state and Python cruft.
.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.DS_Store
